      "body": "Jindal Power Limited, Vedanta Limited (NSEI:VEDL) and Havells India Limited (NSEI:HAVELLS) are among 22 prospective bidders that have submitted expressions of interest (EoIs) to acquire debt-laden Gupta Power Infrastructure Limited, which has admitted debtor claims of INR 42,400 million and is undergoing insolvency proceedings, people aware of the development told ET. The company, which is a manufacturer of cables, wire rods, and conductors, is being resolved under the corporate insolvency resolution process (CIRP). Other interested bidders include UltraTech Cement Limited (NSEI:ULTRACEMCO), Waaree Energies Limited (NSEI:WAAREEENER), Torrent Electricals (TCL Cables Private Limited) and Himadri Speciality Chemical Limited (BSE:500184), Orissa Metaliks Private Limited and Abci Infrastructure",
